[{:adr/consequences ["net-kotobase/MIGRATION.md Phase 3 marked superseded-by-this-ADR\n   (pointing here) instead of describing the dead Kubo-pod plan as\n   actionable" "net-kotobase/docs/USING-AS-A-PIN-SERVICE.md retrieval section corrected\n   to describe actual current state (not yet live)" "ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp's now-doubly-dead 50-infra/vultr/ipfs/ and\n   ipfs-raw/ Helm charts removed, plus any docs describing them as live" "Follow-up needed (separate task, operator with B2 console access, its\n   own ADR in net-kotobase) before ipfs.kotobase.net serves real content:\n   B2 read-only credentials, archiving turned on or backfilled, route\n   cutover"], :adr/authoritative_for ["ipfs.gftd.ai / ipfs.kotobase.net public IPFS retrieval surface: owned by\n    the new gftdcojp/net-kotobase-ipfs repo/Worker, not net-kotobase itself\n    and not any Vultr-hosted Kubo pod" "net-kotobase/MIGRATION.md Phase 3 is superseded by this ADR: the\n    original Phase 3 (reuse the ipfs-origin-proxy -> kubo backend behind\n    ipfs.gftd.ai) assumed a backend that no longer exists"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "net-kotobase-ipfs-gateway-split", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2606120930-murakumo-fleet-stateless-k3s-vultr-winddown.md (lives in ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp/90-docs/adr/, not this superproject)"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607072000-gftdcojp-net-kotobase-ipfs-gateway-split", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-07", :adr/decision "{:summary \"Split IPFS/IPNS retrieval into its own repo/Worker,\\n            gftdcojp/net-kotobase-ipfs, rather than resurrecting the dead\\n            Kubo-pod plan or flipping net-kotobase's whole production\\n            Worker to KOTOBASE_STORAGE_MODE=b2.\", :rationale [\"Blast-radius / privilege separation: ipfs.kotobase.net's only job is a\\n    public unauthenticated GET; it should only ever need read-only B2\\n    credentials, separate from net-kotobase's write-capable B2 creds, CACAO\\n    verification, Stripe billing, and tenant quota state\" \"Doesn't require the ADR-gated whole-Worker mode flip in net-kotobase\\n    itself -- a dedicated retrieval-only Worker can go live without\\n    touching net-kotobase's production storage mode at all\" \"Matches the existing sibling-repo convention for kotobase components\\n    split out of the monolith for a single responsibility\\n    (kotoba-lang/kotobase-cljc-worker, kotoba-lang/kotobase-browser-worker,\\n    kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer)\" \"Matches the owner's explicit naming instruction (gftcojp/net-kotobase-ipfs)\"], :implementation [\"gftdcojp/net-kotobase-ipfs (private, created 2026-07-07):\\n    src/kotobase_ipfs/{sigv4,b2,gateway,worker}.cljc -- a faithful,\\n    read-only-scoped PORT (copied, not depended-on) of net-kotobase's own\\n    clj-edge/src/kotobase/{sigv4,proxy,b2,b2_write}.cljc archive-serving\\n    logic (B2-CAR -> B2-raw -> gateway-fallback -> 404 dispatch, SigV4\\n    signing, content-type sanitization allowlist, gateway SSRF guard).\\n    Copied rather than depended-on so this repo doesn't need net-kotobase's\\n    CACAO/tenant/graph dependency chain just to serve GET /ipfs/*; if the\\n    two drift, net-kotobase's copy (larger test suite) is canonical.\" \"Reads from the SAME B2 bucket/prefix net-kotobase already archives (or\\n    will archive) into (KOTOBASE_B2_PREFIX default kotobase/worker-archive)\\n    -- no separate ingestion path\" \"test/kotobase_ipfs/gateway_test.cljc mirrors net-kotobase's own\\n    worker/test/archive_response_boundary_test.cljc scenarios: 9 tests / 28\\n    assertions, faked global fetch, no network or live B2 calls -- all\\n    passing\" \"shadow-cljs + wrangler.jsonc, CLJC-first per repo-wide runtime priority\\n    convention -- structural template mirrors kotoba-lang/kotobase-cljc-worker\"], :not-decided [\"Whether/when to actually turn on archiving in net-kotobase\\n    (KOTOBASE_B2_ARCHIVE_CIDS=0 as of this writing -- no CID has ever been\\n    archived into B2 by net-kotobase's production Worker). Needs its own\\n    ADR-gate in that repo per its docs/ENVIRONMENT.md. Without it this new\\n    Worker has nothing real to serve yet.\" \"DNS/route cutover for net-kotobase-ipfs: wrangler.jsonc routes left\\n    empty/commented on purpose; no B2 credentials exist for this Worker; no\\n    wrangler deploy has been run.\"]}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"オーナー指示: \\\"ipfs は gftcojp/net-kotobase-ipfs として ipfs に統合\\\" — consolidate\\n           IPFS retrieval as gftdcojp/net-kotobase-ipfs, integrated with the\\n           kotobase.net IPFS surface\", :facts [\"ipfs.gftd.ai was served by Cloudflare Worker ai-gftd-ipfs-proxy (source\\n    repo gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ipfs-proxy no longer exists at all); its GET\\n    /ipfs/<cid> already returned HTTP 530 — backend was a self-hosted Kubo\\n    pod on the Vultr VKE cluster, permanently decommissioned org-wide\\n    (ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp ADR-2606120930). Dead route + Worker script\\n    deleted directly this session.\" \"net-kotobase (kotobase.net) does NOT currently serve public IPFS\\n    retrieval: GET /ipfs/:cid -> 404 \\\"not archived and no gateway\\n    configured\\\" in production (KOTOBASE_STORAGE_MODE=backend,\\n    KOTOBASE_IPFS_GATEWAY_URL unset)\" \"net-kotobase/docs/USING-AS-A-PIN-SERVICE.md names\\n    https://ipfs.gftd.ai/ipfs/<cid> as the retrieval gateway (\\\"backed by the\\n    same store\\\") -- currently false in production\" \"net-kotobase/MIGRATION.md Phase 3 already planned an\\n    ipfs.gftd.ai -> ipfs.kotobase.net cutover, but assumed reusing the SAME\\n    ipfs-origin-proxy -> kubo backend the now-deleted Vultr cluster hosted.\\n    That backend is permanently gone; Phase 3 as originally written cannot\\n    be executed.\" \"net-kotobase's own Worker already has a genuinely working, tested\\n    Worker-native B2 archive mode (KOTOBASE_STORAGE_MODE=b2,\\n    net-kotobase ADR-2606110003): GET /ipfs/* and GET /ipns/* serve CAR/raw\\n    objects from the same B2 bucket net-kotobase uses for CAR-on-B2 pin\\n    durability (net-kotobase ADR-2606042100), gateway-fallback. Never\\n    promoted to production -- net-kotobase docs/ENVIRONMENT.md requires an\\n    explicit ADR + release entry before production leaves\\n    KOTOBASE_STORAGE_MODE=backend, because that flip also switches the\\n    tenant/pin/account control plane off the kotoba backend -- a bigger,\\n    separate decision than \\\"make IPFS retrieval work\\\"\"]}", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/verification ["net-kotobase-ipfs: pnpm test (9 tests / 28 assertions, faked fetch, no\n   network) and pnpm run build (shadow-cljs release worker) both pass" "wrangler deploy --dry-run validates the config without deploying" "no wrangler deploy run for net-kotobase-ipfs (never live)"], :adr/title "ADR-2607072000: gftdcojp — net-kotobase-ipfs, dedicated IPFS/IPNS retrieval Worker (replaces net-kotobase MIGRATION.md Phase 3's dead-Kubo-pod plan)"}]